      "message": "Good catch - thanks!  You\u0027re right that `\u0027b` doesn\u0027t need to be named, because it appears only once in the signature of the function.  OTOH, `\u0027a` needs to appear twice, because if it doesn\u0027t then we\u0027d get:\n\n```\nerror: lifetime may not live long enough\n   --\u003e ../../third_party/skia/experimental/rust_png/ffi/FFI.rs:241:17\n    |\n237 |     fn try_get_iccp(\u0026self, iccp: \u0026mut \u0026[u8]) -\u003e bool {\n    |                     -                 - let\u0027s call the lifetime of this reference `\u00272`\n    |                     |\n    |                     let\u0027s call the lifetime of this reference `\u00271`\n...\n241 |                 *iccp \u003d value;\n    |                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ assignment requires that `\u00271` must outlive `\u00272`\n    |\nhelp: consider introducing a named lifetime parameter and update trait if needed\n    |\n237 |     fn try_get_iccp\u003c\u0027a\u003e(\u0026\u0027a self, iccp: \u0026mut \u0026\u0027a [u8]) -\u003e bool {\n    |                    ++++  ++                   ++\n```\n\nDone.",
